#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson describes the overall flow of the course, and outlines some key components of variational algorithms."
msgstr "Inilalarawan ng araling ito ang pangkalahatang daloy ng kurso, at binabalangkas ang ilang pangunahing bahagi ng mga variational algorithm."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Variational algorithms"
msgstr "Mga variational algorithm"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore infty */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore infty */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course covers the specifics of variational algorithms and near-term hybrid quantum-classical algorithms based on the variational theorem of quantum mechanics. These algorithms can leverage the utility provided by today's non-fault-tolerant quantum computers, making them ideal candidates to achieve <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Practical demonstration of a quantum computer's ability to solve certain computational problems faster than classical computers.\">quantum advantage</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr "Sinasaklaw ng kursong ito ang mga detalye ng mga variational algorithm at near-term hybrid quantum-classical na mga algorithm batay sa variational theorem ng quantum mechanics. Maaaring gamitin ng mga algorithm na ito ang utility na ibinibigay ng mga kasalukuyang non-fault-tolerant na quantum computer, na ginagawa silang mga ideal na kandidato para makamit ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Praktikal na pagpapakita ng kakayahan ng isang quantum computer na malutas ang ilang mga computational problem nang mas mabilis kaysa sa mga klasikal na computer.\">quantum advantage</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Throughout this course, we will explore:\n"
msgstr "Sa buong kurso, tatalakayin natin ang:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each step in the variational algorithm design workflow\n"
msgstr "Bawat hakbang sa workflow ng disenyo ng variational algorithm\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trade-offs associated with each step\n"
msgstr "Mga trade-off na kaugnay ng bawat hakbang\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "How to use [Qiskit Runtime primitives](/guides/primitives) to optimize for speed and accuracy\n"
msgid "How to use [IBM Quantum primitives](/guides/primitives) to optimize for speed and accuracy\n"
msgstr "Paano gamitin ang [Qiskit Runtime primitives](/guides/primitives) para ma-optimize ang bilis at katumpakan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While this course is meant to be a starting place for researchers and developers to explore the utility of quantum computers, feel free to explore the theoretical and foundational knowledge around quantum computing in general in the [Basics of Quantum Information and Computation](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) (also available as [a series of YouTube videos](https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOFEBzvs-VvqKKMXX4vbi4EB1uaErFMSO)).\n"
msgstr "Habang ang kursong ito ay nilalayon bilang panimulang lugar para sa mga mananaliksik at developer na tuklasin ang utility ng mga quantum computer, huwag mag-atubiling tuklasin ang teoretikal at pundasyon na kaalaman sa quantum computing sa pangkalahatan sa [Basics of Quantum Information and Computation](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) (available din bilang [isang serye ng mga YouTube video](https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOFEBzvs-VvqKKMXX4vbi4EB1uaErFMSO)).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simplified hybrid workflow {#simplified-hybrid-workflow}"
msgstr "Simplified hybrid workflow {#simplified-hybrid-workflow}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Flow of a variational algorithm showing steps: initialize problem, prepare ansatz, evaluate cost function, optimize parameters.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/variational-algorithms/variational-workflow.svg)\n"
"Variational algorithms include several modular components that can be combined and optimized based on algorithm, software, and hardware advancements. This includes a *cost function* that describes a specific problem with a set of parameters, an *ansatz* to express the search space with these parameters, and an *optimizer* to iteratively explore the search space. During each iteration, the optimizer evaluates the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A mathematical function used to measure the difference between the predicted output of a model or algorithm and the actual output, with the goal of minimizing this difference through optimization.\">cost function</DefinitionTooltip> with the current parameters and selects the next iteration's parameters until it <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Reaching a stable and optimal solution, where further iterations or modifications to the algorithm no longer result in significant improvements or changes to the solution.\">converges</DefinitionTooltip> on an optimal solution. The hybrid nature of this family of algorithms comes from the fact that the cost functions are evaluated using quantum resources and optimized through classical ones.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Daloy ng isang variational algorithm na nagpapakita ng mga hakbang: initialize problem, prepare ansatz, evaluate cost function, optimize parameters.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/variational-algorithms/variational-workflow.svg)\n"
"Ang mga variational algorithm ay may ilang modular na bahagi na maaaring pagsamahin at ma-optimize batay sa mga pagsulong ng algorithm, software, at hardware. Kasama dito ang isang *cost function* na naglalarawan ng isang tiyak na problema na may set ng mga parameter, isang *ansatz* para ipahayag ang search space gamit ang mga parameter na ito, at isang *optimizer* para paulit-ulit na tuklasin ang search space. Sa bawat iteration, sinusuri ng optimizer ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Isang mathematical function na ginagamit para sukatin ang pagkakaiba sa pagitan ng hinulaang output ng isang modelo o algorithm at ang aktwal na output, na may layuning mabawasan ang pagkakaibang ito sa pamamagitan ng optimization.\">cost function</DefinitionTooltip> gamit ang kasalukuyang mga parameter at pinipili ang mga parameter ng susunod na iteration hanggang sa <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Pagkamit ng isang matatag at optimal na solusyon, kung saan ang karagdagang mga iteration o pagbabago sa algorithm ay hindi na nagreresulta sa mga makabuluhang pagpapabuti o pagbabago sa solusyon.\">mag-converge</DefinitionTooltip> ito sa isang optimal na solusyon. Ang hybrid na katangian ng pamilyang ito ng mga algorithm ay nagmumula sa katotohanan na ang mga cost function ay sinusuri gamit ang mga quantum na resources at na-optimize sa pamamagitan ng mga klasikal na resources.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Initialize problem**: Variational algorithms start by initializing the quantum computer in a _default state_ $|0\\rangle$, then transforming it to some desired (non-parametrized) state $|\\rho\\rangle$, which we will call _reference state_.\n"
msgstr "**I-initialize ang problema**: Ang mga variational algorithm ay nagsisimula sa pamamagitan ng pag-initialize ng quantum computer sa isang _default state_ $|0\\rangle$, pagkatapos ay i-transform ito sa ilang nais na (non-parametrized) na estado $|\\rho\\rangle$, na tatawagin nating _reference state_.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   This transformation is represented by the application of a unitary reference operator $U_R$ on the default state, such that $U_R|0\\rangle = |\\rho\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "   Ang transformation na ito ay kinakatawan ng pagpapatupad ng isang unitary reference operator $U_R$ sa default state, tulad na $U_R|0\\rangle = |\\rho\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Prepare ansatz**: To begin iteratively optimizing from the default state $|0\\rangle$ to the target state $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$, we must define a *variational form* $U_V(\\vec\\theta)$ to represent a collection of parametrized states for our variational algorithm to explore.\n"
msgstr "**Ihanda ang ansatz**: Para magsimulang paulit-ulit na i-optimize mula sa default state $|0\\rangle$ patungo sa target state $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$, dapat nating tukuyin ang isang *variational form* $U_V(\\vec\\theta)$ para kumatawan sa isang koleksyon ng mga parametrized na estado para tuklasin ng ating variational algorithm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   We refer to any particular combination of reference state and variational form as an ansatz, such that: $U_A(\\vec\\theta) := U_V(\\vec\\theta) U_R$. Ansatze will ultimately take the form of parametrized quantum circuits capable of taking the default state $|0\\rangle$ to the target state $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "   Tinutukoy natin ang anumang partikular na kombinasyon ng reference state at variational form bilang ansatz, tulad na: $U_A(\\vec\\theta) := U_V(\\vec\\theta) U_R$. Ang mga ansatze ay magiging anyo ng mga parametrized quantum circuit na kayang dalhin ang default state $|0\\rangle$ sa target state $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   All in all we will have:\n"
msgstr "   Sa kabuuan, magkakaroon tayo ng:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   |0\\rangle \\xrightarrow{U_R} U_R|0\\rangle\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   |0\\rangle \\xrightarrow{U_R} U_R|0\\rangle\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   & = |\\rho\\rangle \\xrightarrow{U_V(\\vec{\\theta})} U_A(\\vec{\\theta})|0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "   & = |\\rho\\rangle \\xrightarrow{U_V(\\vec{\\theta})} U_A(\\vec{\\theta})|0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   & = U_V(\\vec{\\theta})U_R|0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "   & = U_V(\\vec{\\theta})U_R|0\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   & = U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "   & = U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   & = |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "   & = |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "**Evaluate cost function**: We can encode our problem into a _cost function_ $C(\\vec\\theta)$ as a linear combination of Pauli operators, run on a quantum system. While this can be information about a physical system, such as energy or spin, we can also encode non-physical problems as well. We can leverage Qiskit Runtime primitives to address noise with error suppression and mitigation while evaluating our cost function.\n"
msgid "**Evaluate cost function**: We can encode our problem into a _cost function_ $C(\\vec\\theta)$ as a linear combination of Pauli operators, run on a quantum system. While this can be information about a physical system, such as energy or spin, we can also encode non-physical problems as well. We can leverage IBM Quantum primitives to address noise with error suppression and mitigation while evaluating our cost function.\n"
msgstr "**Suriin ang cost function**: Maaari nating i-encode ang aming problema sa isang _cost function_ $C(\\vec\\theta)$ bilang linear na kombinasyon ng mga Pauli operator, na pinapatakbo sa isang quantum system. Habang maaari itong maging impormasyon tungkol sa isang pisikal na sistema, tulad ng enerhiya o spin, maaari rin tayong mag-encode ng mga non-physical na problema. Maaari nating gamitin ang mga Qiskit Runtime primitive para matugunan ang ingay gamit ang error suppression at mitigation habang sinusuri ang ating cost function.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Optimize parameters**: Evaluations are taken to a classical computer, where a classical optimizer analyzes them and chooses the next set of values for the variational parameters. If we have a pre-existing optimal solution, we can set it as an *initial point* $\\vec\\theta_0$ to *bootstrap* our optimization. Using this *initial state* $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta_0)\\rangle$ could help our optimizer find a valid solution faster.\n"
msgstr "**I-optimize ang mga parameter**: Ang mga evaluation ay dinadala sa isang klasikal na computer, kung saan sinusuri ng isang klasikal na optimizer ang mga ito at pinipili ang susunod na set ng mga value para sa mga variational parameter. Kung mayroon tayong pre-existing na optimal na solusyon, maaari nating itakda ito bilang isang *initial point* $\\vec\\theta_0$ para *i-bootstrap* ang ating optimization. Ang paggamit ng *initial state* $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta_0)\\rangle$ na ito ay maaaring makatulong sa ating optimizer na mahanap ang isang valid na solusyon nang mas mabilis.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Adjust ansatz parameters with results, and re-run**: The  entire process is repeated until the classical optimizer's finalization criteria are met, and an optimal set of parameter values $\\vec\\theta^*$ is returned. The proposed solution state for our problem will then be $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta^*)\\rangle = U_A(\\vec\\theta^*)|0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "**I-adjust ang mga ansatz parameter gamit ang mga resulta, at patakbuhin muli**: Ang buong proseso ay inuulit hanggang sa matugunan ang mga finalization criteria ng klasikal na optimizer, at isang optimal na set ng mga parameter value na $\\vec\\theta^*$ ay ibabalik. Ang iminungkahing solution state para sa aming problema ay magiging $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta^*)\\rangle = U_A(\\vec\\theta^*)|0\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Variational theorem {#variational-theorem}"
msgstr "Variational theorem {#variational-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A common goal of variational algorithms is to find the quantum state with the lowest or highest eigenvalue of a certain observable. A key insight we'll use is the _variational theorem_ of quantum mechanics. Before going into its full statement, let us explore some of the mathematical intuition behind it.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang karaniwang layunin ng mga variational algorithm ay ang mahanap ang quantum state na may pinakamababa o pinakamataas na eigenvalue ng isang tiyak na observable. Isang pangunahing insight na gagamitin natin ay ang _variational theorem_ ng quantum mechanics. Bago talakayin ang buong pahayag nito, tuklasin muna natin ang ilang mathematical na intuisyon sa likod nito.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical intuition for energy and ground states {#mathematical-intuition-for-energy-and-ground-states}"
msgstr "Mathematical na intuisyon para sa enerhiya at ground states {#mathematical-intuition-for-energy-and-ground-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In quantum mechanics, energy comes in the form of a quantum observable usually referred to as the _Hamiltonian_, which we'll denote by $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$. Let us consider its <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Process of expressing a matrix as a sum of eigenvalues and eigenvectors, which enables the analysis and manipulation of its properties and behavior.\">spectral decomposition</DefinitionTooltip>:\n"
msgstr "Sa quantum mechanics, ang enerhiya ay nasa anyo ng isang quantum observable na karaniwang tinutukoy bilang _Hamiltonian_, na itatanda natin ng $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$. Isaalang-alang natin ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Proseso ng pagpapahayag ng isang matrix bilang kabuuan ng mga eigenvalue at eigenvector, na nagbibigay-daan sa pagsusuri at pagmamanipula ng mga katangian at gawi nito.\">spectral decomposition</DefinitionTooltip> nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}} = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k |\\phi_k\\rangle \\langle \\phi_k|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}} = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k |\\phi_k\\rangle \\langle \\phi_k|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $N$ is the dimensionality of the space of states, $\\lambda_{k}$ is the $k$-th eigenvalue or, physically, the $k$-th energy level, and $|\\phi_k\\rangle$ is the corresponding <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"State of a physical system in which a magnitude like energy or momentum has a fixed value.\">eigenstate</DefinitionTooltip>: $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\phi_k\\rangle = \\lambda_k |\\phi_k\\rangle$, the expected energy of a system in the (normalized) state $|\\psi\\rangle$ will be:\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $N$ ay ang dimensionality ng space ng mga estado, ang $\\lambda_{k}$ ay ang $k$-th eigenvalue o, sa pisika, ang $k$-th na antas ng enerhiya, at ang $|\\phi_k\\rangle$ ay ang kaukulang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Estado ng isang pisikal na sistema kung saan ang isang magnitude tulad ng enerhiya o momentum ay may nakapirming value.\">eigenstate</DefinitionTooltip>: $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\phi_k\\rangle = \\lambda_k |\\phi_k\\rangle$, ang inaasahang enerhiya ng isang sistema sa (normalized) na estado $|\\psi\\rangle$ ay magiging:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi | \\hat{\\mathcal{H}} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi | \\hat{\\mathcal{H}} | \\psi \\rangle\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\langle \\psi |\\bigg(\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k |\\phi_k\\rangle \\langle \\phi_k|\\bigg) | \\psi \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\langle \\psi |\\bigg(\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k |\\phi_k\\rangle \\langle \\phi_k|\\bigg) | \\psi \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle \\langle \\phi_k| \\psi \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle \\langle \\phi_k| \\psi \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we take into account that $\\lambda_0\\leq \\lambda_k, \\forall k$, we have:\n"
msgstr "Kung isasaalang-alang natin na ang $\\lambda_0\\leq \\lambda_k, \\forall k$, mayroon tayong:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& \\geq  \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_0 |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& \\geq  \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\lambda_0 |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\lambda_0 \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\lambda_0 \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\lambda_0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\lambda_0 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since $\\{|\\phi_k\\rangle \\}_{k=0}^{N-1}$ is an orthonormal basis, the probability of measuring $|\\phi_{k} \\rangle$ is $p_k = |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_{k} \\rangle |^2$, and the sum of all probabilities is such that $\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle|^2 = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}p_k = 1$. In short, the expected energy of any system is higher than the lowest energy or ground state energy:\n"
msgstr "Dahil ang $\\{|\\phi_k\\rangle \\}_{k=0}^{N-1}$ ay isang orthonormal na basis, ang probabilidad ng pagsukat ng $|\\phi_{k} \\rangle$ ay $p_k = |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_{k} \\rangle |^2$, at ang kabuuan ng lahat ng probabilidad ay tulad na $\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} |\\langle \\psi |\\phi_k\\rangle|^2 = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}p_k = 1$. Sa madaling salita, ang inaasahang enerhiya ng anumang sistema ay mas mataas kaysa sa pinakamababang enerhiya o ground state energy:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi | \\hat{\\mathcal{H}} | \\psi \\rangle \\geq \\lambda_0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi | \\hat{\\mathcal{H}} | \\psi \\rangle \\geq \\lambda_0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The above argument applies to any valid (normalized) quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$, so it is perfectly possible to consider parametrized states $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$ that depend on a parameter vector $\\vec\\theta$. This is where the \"variational\" part comes into play. If we consider a cost function given by $C(\\vec\\theta) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$ and want to minimize it, the minimum will always satisfy:\n"
msgstr "Ang argumento sa itaas ay naaangkop sa anumang valid na (normalized) quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$, kaya't ganap na posible na isaalang-alang ang mga parametrized na estado $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$ na nakasalalay sa isang parameter vector $\\vec\\theta$. Dito pumapasok ang bahaging \"variational\". Kung isasaalang-alang natin ang isang cost function na ibinigay ng $C(\\vec\\theta) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$ at nais na i-minimize ito, ang minimum ay palaging magsasatisfy ng:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} C(\\vec\\theta) =\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} \\langle \\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle \\geq \\lambda_0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} C(\\vec\\theta) =\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} \\langle \\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle \\geq \\lambda_0.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The minimum value of $C(\\vec\\theta)$ will be the closest that one can get to $\\lambda_0$ using the parametrized states $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$, and equality will only be reached if there exists a parameter vector $\\vec\\theta^*$ such that $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta^*)\\rangle = |\\phi_0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Ang minimum na value ng $C(\\vec\\theta)$ ang magiging pinakamalapit na maabot sa $\\lambda_0$ gamit ang mga parametrized na estado $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle$, at ang pagkakapantay-pantay ay maaabot lamang kung mayroong isang parameter vector $\\vec\\theta^*$ na tulad na $|\\psi(\\vec\\theta^*)\\rangle = |\\phi_0\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Variational theorem of Quantum Mechanics {#variational-theorem-of-quantum-mechanics}"
msgstr "Variational theorem ng Quantum Mechanics {#variational-theorem-of-quantum-mechanics}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the (normalized) state $|\\psi\\rangle$ of a quantum system depends on a parameter vector $\\vec\\theta$, then the optimal approximation of the ground state (that is, the eigenstate $|\\phi_0\\rangle$ with the minimum eigenvalue $\\lambda_0$) is the one that minimizes the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Average value of a measurement of a quantum system in a particular state, weighted by the probability of the outcome of the state.\">expectation value</DefinitionTooltip> of the Hamiltonian $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$:\n"
msgstr "Kung ang (normalized) na estado $|\\psi\\rangle$ ng isang quantum system ay nakasalalay sa isang parameter vector $\\vec\\theta$, kung gayon ang pinakamainam na approximation ng ground state (ibig sabihin, ang eigenstate $|\\phi_0\\rangle$ na may minimum na eigenvalue na $\\lambda_0$) ay ang nagmi-minimize ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Average na value ng isang measurement ng isang quantum system sa isang partikular na estado, na may timbang ayon sa probabilidad ng kinalabasan ng estado.\">expectation value</DefinitionTooltip> ng Hamiltonian $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\hat{\\mathcal{H}} \\rangle(\\vec\\theta) :=\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec\\theta) |\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}| \\psi(\\vec\\theta) \\rangle \\geq\n"
"\\lambda_0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\hat{\\mathcal{H}} \\rangle(\\vec\\theta) :=\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec\\theta) |\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}| \\psi(\\vec\\theta) \\rangle \\geq\n"
"\\lambda_0\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reason why the variational theorem is stated in terms of energy minima is that it includes a number of mathematical assumptions:\n"
msgstr "Ang dahilan kung bakit ang variational theorem ay nakasaad sa mga tuntunin ng energy minima ay dahil may kasamang bilang ng mga mathematical na pagpapalagay:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For physical reasons, a finite lower bound to the energy $E \\geq \\lambda_0 > -\\infty$ needs to exist, even for $N\\rightarrow\\infty$.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga pisikal na dahilan, dapat may finite na lower bound sa enerhiya $E \\geq \\lambda_0 > -\\infty$, kahit para sa $N\\rightarrow\\infty$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upper bounds do not generally exist.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga upper bound ay karaniwang hindi umiiral.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, mathematically speaking, there is nothing special about the Hamiltonian $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$ beyond these assumptions, so the theorem can be generalized to other quantum observables and their eigenstates provided they follow the same constraints. Also, note that if finite upper bounds exist, the same mathematical arguments could be made for maximizing eigenvalues by swapping lower bounds for upper bounds.\n"
msgstr "Gayunpaman, sa matematika, walang espesyal sa Hamiltonian $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$ lampas sa mga pagpapalagay na ito, kaya ang theorem ay maaaring pangkalahatain sa ibang mga quantum observable at ang kanilang mga eigenstate basta't sumusunod sila sa parehong mga limitasyon. Tandaan din na kung ang mga finite upper bound ay umiiral, ang parehong mga mathematical na argumento ay maaaring gawin para sa pagmaximize ng mga eigenvalue sa pamamagitan ng pagpapalit ng mga lower bound ng mga upper bound.\n"

